  "body": "Show the full path of the shipped post script in the Post dialog's scope\r\nline (top-right weak label), beside the post name:\r\n`Fanuc (built-in) (C:\\...\\assets\\posts\\fanuc.cps)`. A user can now see\r\nwhich post script will run.\r\n\r\nWhat changed\r\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs`: new `posting::post_path(post)` returning the\r\n  shipped `assets/posts/<name>.cps` path for built-in / named registry\r\n  entries (reusing the existing `posting::builtin_post_path`), `None` for a\r\n  user file (its path is already the `post_ref_label`) and for a missing\r\n  registry entry.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/post_dialog.rs`: the scope line appends the path\r\n  suffix for registry entries; user files and missing entries are unchanged.\r\n- `docs/decisions/2292-show-post-path.md`: decision record.\r\n\r\nHow tested\r\n- Pinned by\r\n  `egui_app::post_dialog_tests::post_dialog_shows_the_shipped_post_path`\r\n  (structural: the dialog scope labels the path and the post name).\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 1039 passed, 6 ignored (test count\r\n  unchanged apart from the new pinning test).\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib posting` and `--test posting`: pass.\r\n\r\nNot exercised: the manual GUI verification the maintainer performs (the\r\nprogram header and posted G-code are untouched, so no golden changes).\r\nNo snapshot PNGs change.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Show the shipped post script path in the Post dialog scope line (#2292, PR #2352)\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nScreenshots:\r\nBefore \r\n<img width=\"1052\" height=\"1132\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ccec1848-612e-4944-9d91-c49e7d2cb0f0\" />\r\nAfter, \r\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b11614a3-84e8-445f-b256-85f0199c8892\" />\r\n\r\nFixes #2292\r\n",
